    "durationMs": 211826,
    "finalText": "Done. The URL Shortener API is complete, verified end-to-end, and committed (`fd8caca`).\n\n**Implementation**\n- `app/` — FastAPI app with SQLAlchemy 2.x models, Pydantic schemas, and a `links` router. `DATABASE_URL` is read via pydantic-settings (no hardcoded credentials) and normalized to the `postgresql+psycopg://` driver.\n- `POST /links` — validates the URL manually (absolute http/https with a host) and stores it **unchanged**; validates custom codes against `^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{4,20}$`; generates unique 8-char codes otherwise; 409 on duplicates (check + `IntegrityError` race fallback).\n- `GET /links/{code}`, `GET /links` (ascending by id with `total`), `GET /r/{code}` (302 with exact `Location`, atomic single-row click increment).\n- A `RequestValidationError` handler converts malformed JSON and validation failures into `422 {\"error\": ...}`; 404/409 also use the `error` field.\n- `alembic/` — one autogenerated migration creating the `links` table; `alembic/env.py` pulls the URL from the environment.\n- `start.sh` — runs `alembic upgrade head`, then `exec uvicorn` in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000`. README documents startup.\n\n**Verification**\n- 23/23 pytest cases pass, covering every requirement bullet (422 matrix, 409, 404s, redirect semantics, ordering, click count).\n- Real-HTTP run via `sh start.sh`: fresh-DB migration, correct status codes, case-preserving URLs, clicks incremented exactly once.\n- True restart persistence: killed the server, started a new process — data and click counts survived.\n- Left the environment clean: no server running, `links` table truncated with migrations applied, so the external suite starts fresh."
